+# Captionless native timed hold — bounded acceptance
+
+[Receipt](receipt.json) · [Broad1 run](https://github.com/Siuuuers/dwm/actions/runs/37094251984)
+
+The recovered source is `2937bc569094186dbd1bbefe75efeaa58deccbcc`.
+Actual auxiliary checkout `bee762330520dcf2835df5f725535004a355e015`
+passes all 25 jobs. Its only source-tree addition is the auxiliary workflow;
+its jobs are byte-identical to the canonical workflow. This is not a PR/master
+merge run. Later evidence/documentation descendants are not engine-tested.
+
+13 primary XML reports contain 2,472 executions (2,468 unique script/test pairs),
+207 script executions / 206 unique scripts, no failures/errors/skips. Every test
+name was reconciled with source, including inheritance. Two intentional Settings
+root-refusal reports remain separate: each has 80 expected failures and 3 passes.
+
+The rendered fixture freezes the same timer for 2.509 seconds, emits no text,
+History or speech during the hold, keeps the rail disabled, resumes its remaining
+interval, and requires fresh input for the next real caption. Three retained
+captures were visually inspected. Native regressions separately prove cancellation,
+replacement past the old deadline and stale/duplicate callback retirement.
+The existing native Wait owns timing; no save format or parallel owner was added.
+
+## Reproduce evidence verification
+
+Run `python broad1/verify_package.py` from this directory. It verifies the 11 raw
+parts, complete payload inventory, all 37 original artifact ZIPs and 933 member
+hashes/CRCs without executing Godot or PowerShell. Concatenate the parts in index
+order to unpack `broad1-evidence.tar.gz`. Original ZIPs are retained once under
+`original-artifacts/`; reviews, logs and inventories provide the source bindings.
+Decoded job logs use LF normalization. Artifact ZIP bytes are exact.
+
+The original 98,859,886-byte Windows export ZIP was reconstructed and verified
+separately, including its nested package and binary hashes. Executable/package
+bytes are explicitly excluded from this repository package; raw export reports,
+logs, exact member identities and transport manifest remain. Reconstructing those
+binary bytes later requires the original GitHub artifacts.
+
+## Limits and next work
+
+This is a noncanonical ephemeral hold fixture, not no-Sylvia Hospital completion,
+production timing, mid-hold saving, ordered-ending restore or whole-game acceptance.
+All prior reading/Save/recovery regressions retain their existing bounded scopes.
+The exporter still logs an ObjectDB cleanup warning; editor import has separate
+version-check HTTP403 and cleanup warnings. The actual hold journey logs are clean.
+No global warning-free, leak-free, Windows graphics or accessibility claim follows.
+Performance remains observational and latency is not declared solved.
+
+Next, replace the no-Sylvia notice/Continue contract through the existing Hospital
+command/receipt owner using a noncanonical fixture. Production registration remains
+disabled. All 23 unfinished Beads retain their status/dependencies; no live Dolt
+query or synchronization occurred. PR #1 stays draft and unmerged.
+
+Historical failed red/focused diagnostics and Focus3 packaging remain unchanged.
+Their scopes are not promoted into broad acceptance by this receipt.
